02:30,157:30,177:30,176:15,147:30,136:45,138:30,141:30,224:45,221:40,230:35,250:50,236:55,249:50,248:50,258:65,259:25,268:30,266:30,282:70,279:60,305:100,303:100,298:100,312:100"},{"s":"ghislaine-barthod-chambolle-musigny","n":"Chambolle-Musigny","p":"Domaine Ghislaine Barthod","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Burgundy","a":"Chambolle-Musigny","g":["Pinot Noir"],"pr":130,"abv":13,"e":"Destemmed; about 16 months in barrel, roughly a quarter new","sv":"14–16°C","d":"30 minutes when young","w":"5–18 years","ds":"Chambolle at its most perfumed: violet, rose and iris lift above raspberry and red cherry, with a cool limestone backbone. The tannins feel like silk, the frame is light, and the precision is entirely Barthod''s.","x":"284:2,285:70,286:45,287:47,288:45,289:65,290:70,291:20,292:0,293:18,1:75,3:65,5:45,6:30,8:20,71:90,72:60,81:45,82:35,84:20,138:35,136:30,148:20,135:15,124:10,212:85,214:40,236:90,252:95,254:65,249:65,240:60,243:45,258:70,259:20,260:35,282:80,279:60,299:100,298:100,310:100,297:100"},{"s":"comte-armand-pommard-clos-des-epeneaux","n":"Pommard Premier Cru Clos des Epeneaux","p":"Domaine du Comte Armand","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Burgundy","a":"Pommard Premier Cru","g":["Pinot Noir"],"pr":190,"abv":13.5,"e":"Mostly destemmed; 18–24 months in French oak, a minority new; biodynamic monopole","sv":"15–17°C","d":"1–2 hours when young","w":"8–25 years","ds":"Pommard''s muscular reputation in its most complete form: black cherry, blackberry and plum over iron, red clay and a dark spice edge. The tannins are dense and the frame is architectural, so it needs years before its brooding fruit turns savory.","x":"284:2,285:65,286:75,287:52,288:72,289:75,290:78,291:35,292:0,293:18,14:80,12:45,15:45,1:35,2:25,71:30,143:50,152:45,151:45,148:35,188:25,126:25,123:15,135:25,170:15,157:20,216:65,214:40,227:30,237:75,245:90,255:65,251:50,242:45,258:70,259:30,282:95,279:65,294:100,297:100,295:100,299:100,315:100"},{"s":"comtes-lafon-meursault","n":"Meursault","p":"Domaine de