","sv":"11–13°C","d":"1 hour when young","w":"8–25 years","ds":"The summit of Chablis: lemon, quince and yellow apple compressed into a dense, saline core of chalk, flint and crushed shell. Old feuillettes add texture without any oak flavor, and it is austere in youth before slowly turning to beeswax and honeyed complexity over decades.","x":"284:2,285:88,286:3,287:52,288:65,289:82,290:90,291:20,292:0,293:18,34:65,40:45,43:30,47:40,46:30,49:30,51:20,53:25,85:30,73:15,144:80,138:85,137:60,141:65,136:55,158:20,203:20,193:15,192:10,230:75,223:25,255:80,237:60,249:85,243:95,245:80,248:75,239:40,258:90,260:70,282:95,279:70,305:100,306:100,303:100,298:100,315:100"},{"s":"domaine-dujac-clos-de-la-roche","n":"Clos de la Roche Grand Cru","p":"Domaine Dujac","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Burgundy","a":"Clos de la Roche Grand Cru","g":["Pinot Noir"],"pr":650,"abv":13.5,"e":"Largely whole-cluster fermentation; about 18 months in barrel, mostly new","sv":"15–17°C","d":"1–2 hours when young","w":"10–30 years","ds":"Dujac''s whole-cluster signature on Morey''s greatest vineyard: red and black cherry, rose and violet, then a seductive layer of cinnamon, five-spice and tea from the stems. Silky yet deeply structured, it moves from exotic perfume in youth to forest-floor depth with age.","x":"284:2,285:68,286:62,287:52,288:62,289:82,290:88,291:50,292:0,293:20,1:70,14:60,3:45,5:35,9:30,72:55,71:50,197:20,124:30,123:25,134:30,114:25,148:45,151:35,143:30,140:25,157:30,158:15,156:15,212:70,214:55,248:85,252:75,245:65,236:75,255:60,262:85,259:50,282:95,279:60,297:100,299:100,310:100,298:100"},{"s":"billecart-salmon-brut-rose","n":"Brut Rosé","p":"Billecart-Salmon","t":"sparkling","c":"France","r":"Champagne","a":"Champagne","g":["Chardonnay","Pinot Noir","Meunier"],"pr":100,"abv":12,"e":"Rosé d''assemblage with a small addition of Pinot Noir red wine; cold-settled, cool fermentation in stainless steel; about 3 years on lees","sv":"8–10°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–5 years","ds":"The pale, ethereal rosé every house measures itself against: wild strawberry, raspberry and red currant with a hint of rose and citrus zest, carried on an exceptionally fine mousse. More about delicacy and freshness than autolytic depth, it is finished with chalky, pinpoint precision.","x":"284:8,285:82,286:4,287:40,288:42,289:60,290:65,291:0,292:92,293:25,5:70,3:60,6:40,1:25,38:20,40:40,72:40,85:20,138:45,136:25,178:30,183:25,180:20,202:15,233:85,228:60,221:30,236:90,254:60,240:85,249:65,247:55,272:95,261:70,279:60,283:75,323:100,304:100,307:100,299:100"},{"s":"krug-grande-cuvee","n":"Grande Cuvée Brut","p":"Krug","t":"sparkling","c":"France","r":"Champagne","a":"Champagne","g":["Pinot Noir","Chardonnay","Meunier"],"pr":260,"abv":12,"e":"Base wines fermented in small old oak casks; blend of over 120 wines from more than ten vintages; about 7 years on lees","sv":"9–11°C","d":"Not needed; serve in a wide white-wine glass","w":"Now–20 years","ds":"A prestige cuvée built on a deep reserve library rather than one vintage: baked apple, quince and candied citrus fold into toasted brioche, roasted hazelnut, honey and gingerbread. Immense yet fresh and finely beaded, with a finish that seems to go on forever.","x":"284:7,285:78,286:4,287:42,288:72,289:88,290:92,291:30,292:92,293:50,47:50,33:35,49:35,51:30,43:40,31:30,39:20,32:15,178:75,184:65,183:35,180:35,203:75,202:35,205:25,192:35,200:25,135:25,158:15,138:35,141:25,233:80,221:60,248:95,238:65,237:60,257:55,245:55,272:95,260:55,280:60,282:85,323:100,305:100,298:100,315:100,310:100"},{"s":"e-guigal-cote-rotie-brune-et-blonde","n":"Côte-Rôtie Brune et Blonde","p":"E. Guigal","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Northern Rhône","a":"Côte-Rôtie","g":["Syrah","Viognier"],"pr":80,"abv":13.5,"e":"About 36 months in oak barrels, roughly 40% new","sv":"16–18°C","d":"1 hour","w":"5–20 years from vintage","ds":"Guigal''s blend of the schist-dark Côte Brune and the paler, granite-and-silt Côte Blonde: blackberry and black cherry lifted by violet, a dab of co-fermented Viognier, cracked pepper and smoked bacon. Long barrel ageing rounds the edges without dulling the pepper.","x":"284:2,285:60,286:65,287:55,288:70,289:75,290:75,291:55,292:0,293:30,12:70,14:60,15:40,71:65,55:10,120:70,112:50,190:60,126:30,143:30,156:30,157:30,158:35,148:20,185:20,214:60,231:40,252:60,242:60,258:75,236:50,259:40,282:75,280:40,295:100,299:100,297:100,315:100"},{"s":"domaine-jean-louis-chave-hermitage-rouge","n":"Hermitage Rouge","p":"Domaine Jean-Louis Chave","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Northern Rhône","a":"Hermitage","g":["Syrah"],"pr":400,"abv":13.5,"e":"Around 18 months in oak barrels, roughly 15–20% new; blended from several Hermitage lieux-dits","sv":"16–18°C","d":"2–3 hours when young","w":"15–40 years from vintage","ds":"The reference point for Hermitage, assembled from parcels across the hill so granite, loess and limestone each add a layer. Dense blackberry and cassis, black pepper, olive and smoked meat sit over a graphite-and-iron core, framed by abundant but finely ground tannin. Closed in youth, it rewards decades.","x":"284:2,285:65,286:85,287:60,288:85,289:85,290:95,291:35,292:0,293:20,12:80,14:55,13:40,15:45,71:50,120:75,112:50,190:55,142:60,140:55,143:40,126:35,198:20,185:20,150:15,188:20,214:75,216:40,227:35,245:95,237:70,248:85,258:90,251:55,255:75,260:45,282:100,279:55,295:100,294:100,297:100,310:100,315:100"},{"s":"m-chapoutier-chante-alouette-hermitage-blanc","n":"Chante-Alouette Hermitage Blanc","p":"M. Chapoutier","t":"white","c":"France","r":"Northern Rhône","a":"Hermitage","g":["Marsanne"],"pr":110,"abv":14,"e":"Fermented and aged partly in oak barrels and partly in vat, about 10 months on fine lees","sv":"12–14°C","d":"30–60 minutes","w":"Now–20 years; often goes quiet from about year 4 to 8","ds":"Pure Marsanne from Hermitage''s sandy upper slopes: quince, ripe pear and acacia over a seam of bitter almond and beeswax. Low acidity is balanced by sheer extract, so the texture is broad and waxy rather than flabby, and with age it moves toward honey and toasted hazelnut.","x":"284:3,285:40,286:5,287:65,288:85,289:70,290:80,291:30,292:0,293:20,51:55,49:50,54:40,55:35,73:50,74:40,202:55,203:30,193:45,192:35,100:20,127:20,136:35,141:20,222:70,223:55,224:60,238:60,250:50,248:50,260:35,266:30,282:75,279:40,305:100,298:100,312:100,303:100,315:100"},{"s":"auguste-clape-cornas","n":"Cornas","p":"Auguste Clape","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Northern Rhône","a":"Cornas","g":["Syrah"],"pr":150,"abv":13,"e":"Whole-bunch fermentation in concrete, then 18–22 months in large old foudres","sv":"16–18°C","d":"2 hours or more","w":"10–30 years from vintage","ds":"Old-school Cornas from old granite terraces, fermented with stems and never touched by new wood. Blackberry and violet are wrapped in black olive, cracked pepper, smoked meat and an iron, almost bloody, savoury streak. The tannins are firm and a little rustic in youth and need years to settle.","x":"284:2,285:70,286:85,287:50,288:80,289:80,290:85,291:10,292:0,293:20,12:75,14:45,15:30,21:30,71:45,120:80,112:60,190:70,188:40,143:55,140:40,151:40,126:30,198:30,185:30,216:70,218:35,227:50,242:85,245:85,246:50,239:45,258:90,251:60,262:65,260:70,278:50,282:95,279:50,297:100,295:100,294:100,301:100"},{"s":"domaine-pierre-gonon-saint-joseph-rouge","n":"Saint-Joseph Rouge","p":"Domaine Pierre Gonon","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Northern Rhône","a":"Saint-Joseph","g":["Syrah"],"pr":75,"abv":13,"e":"Whole-cluster fermentation, aged in old demi-muids and foudres","sv":"15–17°C","d":"1 hour","w":"5–20 years from vintage","ds":"Saint-Joseph from the granite hillsides around Mauves, made the old way with whole bunches and old wood. It is all about perfume and savour: black raspberry and violet, a lot of black and white pepper, olive and a faint smokiness, carried on bright acidity and fine, slightly stemmy tannin.","x":"284:2,285:68,286:60,287:45,288:60,289:70,290:75,291:10,292:0,293:15,21:50,12:55,14:40,9:35,71:60,120:80,121:30,112:55,113:20,190:50,143:35,140:45,111:25,126:15,214:60,229:45,230:40,242:80,240:60,252:55,249:55,258:70,262:75,260:70,265:30,282:70,279:60,295:100,299:100,301:100,296:100"},{"s":"domaine-alain-graillot-crozes-hermitage-rouge","n":"Crozes-Hermitage Rouge","p":"Domaine Alain Graillot","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Northern Rhône","a":"Crozes-Hermitage","g":["Syrah"],"pr":40,"abv":13,"e":"Whole-cluster fermentation, about 12 months in older barrels","sv":"15–17°C","d":"30 minutes","w":"Now–10 years","ds":"The bottle that showed Crozes could be serious: crunchy black raspberry and blackberry, violets and cracked pepper, with a light olive-and-bacon note from whole-cluster fermentation. Juicy and supple enough for a weeknight, but it has the structure to improve for a few years.","x":"284:2,285:62,286:50,287:50,288:55,289:65,290:60,291:15,292:0,293:15,21:55,12:60,14:50,9:30,71:50,120:70,112:45,190:40,106:15,126:20,140:25,214:50,229:60,231:45,240:65,242:60,256:55,258:60,262:60,260:55,279:75,283:45,300:100,302:100,295:100,301:100"},{"s":"georges-vernay-condrieu-les-terrasses-de-l-empire","n":"Condrieu Les Terrasses de l''Empire","p":"Domaine Georges Vernay","t":"white","c":"France","r":"Northern Rhône","a":"Condrieu","g":["Viognier"],"pr":85,"abv":14,"e":"About 10 months on lees, roughly half in barrel and half in tank","sv":"10–12°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–6 years","ds":"Viognier from the house that saved Condrieu: ripe apricot, white peach and honeysuckle, with orange blossom and a hint of ginger. The texture is oily and broad, but a granite-derived stoniness on the finish keeps the perfume from becoming cloying.","x":"284:4,285:38,286:3,287:65,288:75,289:85,290:70,291:20,292:0,293:10,55:90,53:60,54:40,41:25,74:70,75:50,71:20,85:40,129:20,127:15,140:30,177:20,223:60,224:65,221:40,252:90,238:60,241:50,236:45,266:30,260:25,279:80,283:60,305:100,308:100,298:100,318:100"},{"s":"chateau-de-beaucastel-chateauneuf-du-pape-rouge","n":"Châteauneuf-du-Pape Rouge","p":"Château de Beaucastel","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Southern Rhône","a":"Châteauneuf-du-Pape","g":["Mourvèdre","Grenache","Syrah","Counoise","Cinsault"],"pr":110,"abv":14.5,"e":"Grapes briefly flash-heated before fermentation; about 12 months in large old oak foudres","sv":"16–18°C","d":"2 hours when young","w":"8–30 years from vintage","ds":"A Mourvèdre-heavy Châteauneuf using all thirteen permitted varieties, so it is more savoury and gamey than most of its neighbours. Kirsch and blackberry give way to garrigue, leather, licorice and an animal, sometimes farmyard, edge that becomes truffle and tobacco with age. Muscular and slow to develop.","x":"284:3,285:55,286:75,287:75,288:85,289:85,290:85,291:15,292:0,293:25,27:55,14:50,12:55,15:45,22:15,106:70,78:20,102:30,112:35,126:40,185:50,188:50,155:25,190:25,186:30,150:25,148:30,143:20,216:55,227:50,242:75,237:65,248:80,258:85,251:50,245:70,260:70,282:95,280:35,297:100,295:100,294:100,310:100,315:100"}]'::jsonb);
